Variables & Scope:
public class ScopeDemo {
    static int classVar = 1;      // static: shared across all instances
    String instanceVar = "obj";    // instance: one per object

    public void demo() {
        int local = 10;            // local: must initialize
        if (local > 0) {
            String blockVar = "block"; // block-scoped
            System.out.println(blockVar);
        }
        // System.out.println(blockVar); // ❌ out of scope
    }
}

Type Casting:
// Widening — automatic, no data loss
int small = 100;
long big = small;           // int → long (implicit)
double d = big;             // long → double (implicit)

// Narrowing — explicit cast required
double pi = 3.14159;
int truncated = (int) pi;   // truncates fractional part → 3
long val = 1_000_000_000_000L;
int narrowed = (int) val;   // data may be lost!

// Reference casting
Object obj = "Hello";               // upcast: String → Object (auto)
String str = (String) obj;          // downcast: Object → String (explicit)
// Integer num = (Integer) obj;     // ❌ ClassCastException at runtime

